      "notes": [
        "Each shaman occupies 72 consecutive cells laid out as 16 idle, 32 walk, 24 cast. All twelve blocks score exactly on the reversed cell-width signature, which is what fixed the 16/32/24 split rather than eyeballing it.",
        "The four groups start at 200, 272, 351 and 423, and their headdresses differ: feathers, feathers, a sun disc and leaves. The colours still run blue, red, yellow, green, the same order as the braves and firewarriors, so they are read as the four tribes' shamans.",
        "The two halves differ in cell height, 35 to 36 against 39, and a seven-cell sparkle sits between them at 344. Whether that makes them two unit types rather than four variants of one is unresolved."
      ]
